# SuperconX Billboard — firmware {{VERSION}}

Native ESP32-S3 firmware for the Supercon 10 "Billboard Badge", built with
ESP-IDF v5.4.2. This version string is embedded in the firmware (`PROJECT_VER`)
so the badge and the web flasher both report `{{VERSION}}`.

## ⚠️ This is an APP-ONLY release

These artifacts contain the **bootloader + partition table + factory app only**.
They do **not** include the LittleFS `storage` image (gallery artwork, schedule,
and the TinyStories model/tokenizer). Those are third-party assets that are not
yet cleared for redistribution, so the `storage` partition (`0x310000`) ships
empty. The firmware boots and mounts an empty `/data`; asset-backed apps will be
blank until a future full-image release.

## Flashing (user-initiated)

Nothing here flashes your badge automatically — every path below is something
**you** choose to run. The badge is fully open (no secure boot / flash
encryption), so you can always go back.

**Easiest — ESP Web Tools:** host `manifest.json` next to the other assets and
open it with an ESP Web Tools install button, or any installer that accepts a
manifest URL. It writes the three component parts to an ESP32-S3.

**One-shot full image (esptool):**

```
esptool.py --chip esp32s3 write_flash 0x0 superconx-billboard-{{VERSION}}-merged.bin
```

**Manual component flash (esptool):**

```
esptool.py --chip esp32s3 write_flash \
  0x0      bootloader.bin \
  0x8000   partition-table.bin \
  0x10000  superconx-billboard-{{VERSION}}-factory.bin
```

Verify downloads against `SHA256SUMS`:

```
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
```

## Restoring the stock badge

This firmware replaces the stock LVGL-MicroPython "Billboard Badge" image. To go
back, reflash your own full dump as described in
[BADGE_REPORT.md](BADGE_REPORT.md) ("Restore to stock"):

```
esptool.py --port /dev/tty.usbmodemXXXX write_flash 0 dump/badge_full_8MB.bin
```

(The stock dump is personal to your badge and is not distributed here.)

## How these artifacts were validated in CI

- `esptool image_info` parses the merged image and the factory app.
- The factory app's embedded version equals `{{VERSION}}`.
- `manifest.json` parses, and every referenced part exists at an offset that
  matches `native_firmware/partitions.csv` (factory `@0x10000`).
- A QEMU 9.2.2 boot smoke (Espressif QEMU, via `emulator/emu.py`) boots the same
  tagged source and confirms it reaches `app_main()` and mounts `/data` with no
  panic or reboot.

## Assets

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `superconx-billboard-{{VERSION}}-merged.bin` | Full image, flash at `0x0` (app-only) |
| `bootloader.bin` | Component part `@0x0` |
| `partition-table.bin` | Component part `@0x8000` |
| `superconx-billboard-{{VERSION}}-factory.bin` | Factory app `@0x10000` |
| `manifest.json` | ESP Web Tools manifest |
| `SHA256SUMS` | SHA-256 of every asset above |
